# Coach-Client Assignment Field Consistency

## Three Assignment Fields (Must Stay in Sync)

Client profiles have THREE fields that indicate coach assignment. All three must be set consistently:

| Field | Value | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `coach_id` | `COACH_COACHN_ID` | Primary assignment (hardware ID of coach) |
| `assigned_coach_id` | `COACH_COACHN_ID` | Legacy field checked by `coach_get_clients` |
| `assigned_coach` | `CoachN` | Username-based lookup (used as fallback) |

The `coach_get_clients` handler checks all three fields plus session history. If any field is missing or stale, the client won't appear in the coach portal.

## When Assigning a Client to a Coach

Always update all three fields atomically:

```sql
UPDATE users SET profile_data = jsonb_set(
  jsonb_set(
    jsonb_set(profile_data, '{coach_id}', '"COACH_COACHN_ID"'),
    '{assigned_coach_id}', '"COACH_COACHN_ID"'
  ),
  '{assigned_coach}', '"CoachN"'
)
WHERE username = $1 AND role = 'CLIENT';
```

After DB update, restart `nate_bridge` to reload the in-memory registry cache.

## Default Coach Assignment

All new clients are assigned to **CoachN** (`COACH_COACHN_ID`) until further notice. This applies to:
- New client registrations (via `register_new_user()` in `bridge_server.py`)
- Clients without an assigned coach
- Any client previously assigned to DrNevedal1 (admin should never be a coach)

When modifying `register_new_user()`, always verify all three fields (`coach_id`, `assigned_coach_id`, `assigned_coach`) are set with consistent defaults. The old default was `hnevedal`/`COACH_HNEVEDAL_ID` — this is retired. Never revert to it.

## Coach View Filters

The coach portal has 5 filter modes. All operate on the same `_clients` list:

| Filter | Shows |
|---|---|
| All | All clients grouped by family/company, individuals separate |
| Clients | Every client as an individual row (no family grouping) |
| Families | Only clients with a `family_id`, grouped by family |
| Coach-Only | Only `COACH_ONLY` tier clients |
| Company | Only clients with a `company_id`, grouped by company |

## Assistant Coach Visibility

When a coach is an assistant (via `coach_hierarchy` table), `coach_get_clients` also returns clients assigned to their master coach(es). This ensures assistants can view and schedule sessions for the master's clients.

## Session Creation Uses Individual Client IDs

Live sessions are always keyed to `client_id` (individual), not `family_id`. The `family_id` is optional metadata for grouping. Coaches can schedule sessions for any individual client regardless of family membership.
